WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:06.180
Mō tātou, a, mō ka uri a muri ake nei

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:16.720
If you’ve visited the Regeneration Reserves
area recently, you will have noticed the huge

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.050
changes taking place here.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.279
All this activity is known as the 'enabling
works'.

00:00:21.279 --> 00:00:24.760
It’s getting everything prepared for the
various recreational facilities that will

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.960
be constructed here, and it’s got three
main components.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.750
The first work package is the Beswick Storm
Management Water area, that is the installation

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.970
of a new storm water basin.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.210
The second package is the earthworks that
you can see going on behind me here.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:45.160
So it’s the importation of about 50,000
cubes of fill, to create a level playing field

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.260
for the new sports pitches.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.740
And the third work component is the decommissioning
of the roads and utilities.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.940
The scale of the work is huge, and expected
to take about eight months.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:01.920
Overlapping that, construction of the facilities
such as the sports fields, dog parks and BMX

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.680
track will be getting underway.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.200
Trent Jones grew up riding on the old Kaiapoi BMX
track, before eventually representing New

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.390
Zealand in BMX at the Rio Olympics.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:16.210
He’s currently overseeing the rebuild of
the North Canterbury BMX Club track, and will

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.450
design the new track in Kaiapoi.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:22.550
To the general eye, it’s just looks like
some dirt and some piles here and some piles

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:29.320
there, but the shapes and the design and final
features are very specific to our sport.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:34.220
The proposed track will be wide enough for
four bikes at a time and Trent has some key

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:36.130
factors driving his design.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:42.360
My first thought it fun, that’s obviously
the endgoal – to have has much fun as possible.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:49.140
Safety is the second one and then being able
to cater for that wide spread of skill level.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:53.700
You’ve got everyone from five and under
all the way through to 55 plus that can attend

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.820
and have that thrill of riding the bike and
challenging themselves.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:02.340
Construction of the BMX track is scheduled
to start early in the new year.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.210
While we’re aware this area has been popular
for walking and cycling, it’s really important

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:10.890
that people stay clear of the worksite – for
their own safety and the safety of our contractors.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:14.140
We'll take another look at progress here and
at the Marine Precinct

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:15.860
in our next update.

